CAT = "nzfkLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
# Health and Safety at Work Act 2015 and the GRWM Regulations 2016 as they bear on forklift work.
Q = [
("A labour-hire operator drives at a client's warehouse. Who owes them a primary duty of care?",
 'Both the hire firm and the client', ['Only the labour-hire firm', "Only the client's site manager", 'Only the operator themself'],
 'Section 36 covers workers who work for the PCBU and workers whose work the PCBU influences or directs, so both PCBUs hold the duty. Section 34 requires PCBUs with the same duty to consult each other.'),
('Which HSWA standard limits how far a PCBU must go to keep forklift work safe?',
 'So far as reasonably practicable', ['As far as the budget allows', 'Only as far as the operator asks', 'As far as the insurer requires'],
 'Section 36 duties apply so far as is reasonably practicable. Section 22 weighs the likelihood and harm of the risk, what is known about it and the ways to control it, and only then cost, which may count only if grossly disproportionate.'),
('A barrier costs little and greatly cuts a serious forklift risk. Can its cost justify leaving it out?',
 "No, it isn't disproportionate", ['Yes, any cost can justify it', 'Yes, once the budget is spent', 'Only if the operator agrees'],
 'Section 22 lets cost count only after weighing the risk and the controls, and only if the cost is grossly disproportionate to the risk. A cheap control for a serious risk is reasonably practicable.'),
('A worker is told to wear a seatbelt on every counterbalanced forklift. Which HSWA duty requires them to comply?',
 'Duties of workers, section 45', ['Duty of officers, section 44', 'Duty to notify, section 56', 'Duty to preserve sites, section 55'],
 "Section 45 requires a worker to take reasonable care for their own and others' safety and to comply, as far as reasonably able, with reasonable instructions from the PCBU."),
('A visiting truck driver walks into a marked forklift zone. What does the Act require of them?',
 'Reasonable care for their own safety', ['Nothing, as they are not a worker', 'Only what their own firm says', "To sign the site's forklift register"],
 'Section 46 gives other persons at a workplace a duty to take reasonable care for their own safety and not to put others at risk, and to comply with reasonable instructions.'),
('Under the GRWM Regulations, which control comes first when the forklift hazard cannot be eliminated?',
 'Isolation or engineering', ['Personal protective equipment', 'Warning signs and site rules', 'Refresher training for drivers'],
 'Regulation 6 sets the order: substitute, isolate or engineer first; then administrative controls for any remaining risk; then PPE last.'),
('A site paints walkways and keeps forklifts on separate aisles with barriers. Which kind of control are the barriers?',
 'Isolating the hazard', ['Administrative control', 'Substitution', 'Personal protective equipment'],
 'Physical barriers that keep people away from the trucks isolate the hazard. Painted lines and rules alone are administrative controls, which regulation 6 places lower.'),
('Which control sits lowest in the GRWM hierarchy for forklift risks?',
 'Hi-vis vests and safety boots', ['Barrier rails between aisles', 'A one-way traffic system', 'Replacing a diesel truck with electric'],
 'PPE is the last line under regulation 6, used only for the risk left after higher controls. Barriers isolate, and a quieter electric truck is substitution.'),
('A new operator has no forklift experience. What must the PCBU ensure under regulation 9 before they work alone?',
 'Training or supervision', ['A class 2 driver licence', "Five years' work at the site", "A doctor's fitness letter"],
 'Regulation 9 requires a worker using plant to have adequate knowledge and experience or be supervised by someone who has it, and to be adequately trained in its safe use.'),
('Forklift training must be readily understandable to the trainee. Which regulation says so?',
 'GRWM regulation 9', ['Section 56 of the Act', 'GRWM regulation 47', 'GRWM regulation 25'],
 'Regulation 9(3) requires the PCBU to ensure, so far as reasonably practicable, that training is readily understandable by any person it is given to.'),
('What is the youngest age at which a worker may drive a forklift at work under the GRWM Regulations?',
 '15', ['12', '16', '18'],
 'Regulation 47 bars workers under 15 from driving self-propelled mobile plant such as a forklift. The 12-year exception covers only trained workers on tractors used for agricultural work.'),
('A 13-year-old worker on a farm asks to drive the yard forklift. What applies?',
 'Not allowed under 15', ['Allowed with training', 'Allowed off the public road', 'Allowed if supervised'],
 'The under-15 ban in regulation 47 covers self-propelled mobile plant over 700 kg. Its exception for those aged 12 and over covers only tractors in agricultural work, not forklifts.'),
('Regulation 47 does not count small self-propelled machinery as a vehicle. What mass sets that line?',
 '700 kg', ['350 kg', '1,000 kg', '3,500 kg'],
 "Regulation 47(3) excludes machinery with a mass of 700 kg or less from 'vehicle'. Forklifts are far heavier, so the under-15 driving ban applies."),
('A worker believes driving a forklift with a cracked fork would expose them to serious immediate risk. What may they do?',
 'Refuse the work and tell the PCBU', ['Use it and report it at shift end', 'Keep working until a supervisor agrees', 'Refuse but tell nobody'],
 'Section 83 lets a worker cease or refuse work that would expose them to a serious risk from immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard. They must notify the PCBU as soon as practicable.'),
('After refusing unsafe forklift work, what must the worker try next to keep refusing?',
 'Try to resolve it with the PCBU', ['Report it straight to Police', 'Find another forklift to use', 'Wait until the next shift'],
 'Section 83(2) lets a worker continue refusing if they try to resolve it with the PCBU as soon as practicable, it stays unresolved, and they still reasonably believe the risk is serious.'),
('Who must notify WorkSafe after a notifiable event involving a forklift?',
 'The PCBU', ['The injured worker', 'The forklift dealer', 'The nearest bystander'],
 'Section 56 puts the duty on the PCBU to ensure the regulator is notified as soon as possible after becoming aware of a notifiable event.'),
('How must a PCBU notify WorkSafe of a notifiable event?',
 'Fastest means available', ['By post within a month', 'In the annual safety report', 'Only on a written form'],
 'Section 56(2) allows telephone or writing, including email, but it must be by the fastest possible means in the circumstances.'),
("From when is a PCBU's five-year record of a notifiable event counted?",
 'When notice was given to WorkSafe', ['When the forklift was bought', 'When the injured worker returns', 'When the inspector closes the file'],
 'Section 57 requires the record to be kept for at least 5 years from the date on which notice of the event was given to the regulator under section 56.'),
('After a notifiable forklift event, what may still be done before an inspector authorises it?',
 'Helping the injured person', ['Repairing the forklift', 'Restacking the fallen load', 'Hosing down the area'],
 'Section 55 says the site must not be disturbed until an inspector authorises it, but allows action to help an injured person, make the site safe or prevent a further event.'),
('A load falls from raised forks and nearly hits a worker. Which category of event can this be?',
 'Notifiable incident', ['Notifiable illness', 'Routine near miss only', 'Plant registration breach'],
 'Section 24 lists the uncontrolled fall or release from a height of any plant, substance or thing that exposes a person to a serious risk from immediate exposure as a notifiable incident.'),
("A worker must service a mast with the carriage raised. What does regulation 24 require if the risk can't be eliminated?",
 "Supports so it can't fall", ['A second person watching', 'Hi-vis clothing for both', 'Working only in daylight'],
 'Regulation 24 requires supports or other devices under a raised object so it cannot fall or be lowered while a person is under it.'),
("Stock could fall from high racking while forklifts work. If it can't be prevented or caught, what does regulation 25 call for?",
 'A no-entry exclusion zone', ['Hard hats for drivers only', 'A sign asking for care', 'Slower lifting speeds'],
 'Regulation 25 requires measures to stop objects falling freely, then a system to arrest the fall, and if neither is practicable an exclusion zone persons are prohibited from entering.'),
('A worker is given safety boots for the loading dock. What must they do if the boots are damaged?',
 'Tell the PCBU', ['Glue them and carry on', 'Buy new ones themselves', 'Keep wearing them as issued'],
 'Regulation 18 requires a worker to wear PPE as instructed, not misuse it, and inform the PCBU of any damage, defect or need to clean it.'),
('A company director never visits the warehouse. Which duty must they still meet for forklift safety?',
 'Due diligence as an officer', ['None, as they are not a worker', 'Only to sign the annual report', 'To hold a forklift certificate'],
 'Section 44 requires officers to exercise due diligence to ensure the PCBU complies with its duties, whether or not they visit the site.'),
]
